abstract: >-
  Computational audit of genome-editing readouts with finite-record
  identification bounds, explicit sequence correspondence and target-relative
  alignment certificates. Version 0.7.0 introduced complete retained COL17A1 spans,
  pair ledgers, all-target score witnesses, an independent bounded path oracle,
  a unified reproduction entry point, an epistemic evidence graph and verified
  historical evidence archives. Version 0.8.1 places the historical evidence
  inside the Git tree for complete GitHub-to-Zenodo source archiving. Computational replay does not establish
  independent molecular truth or biological accuracy. Original source studies
  retain attribution and data terms; code licenses are explicitly scoped.
  Manuscript and formal supplementary text are excluded until the author
  confirms bioRxiv acceptance.
keywords:
  - "genome editing readouts"
  - "observability"
  - "partial identification"
  - "sequence correspondence"
  - "CFTR F508del"

repository-code: "https://github.com/FacundoFirmenich/crispr-observability"
